# Pre-Commit Checklist

## Before Every Commit, Verify:

### 1. Documentation Alignment
- [ ] Change aligns with documented design in `docs/lld/`
- [ ] If design changed, documentation is updated
- [ ] New features have user story in `docs/product/epics/`

### 2. Test Coverage
- [ ] Unit tests for business logic
- [ ] Integration tests for external dependencies
- [ ] Tests actually test the behavior, not just call methods
- [ ] All new code paths have test coverage

### 3. Error Handling
- [ ] No empty catch blocks
- [ ] Domain exceptions used (not generic Exception)
- [ ] Error messages are helpful for debugging
- [ ] Sensitive info not leaked in error responses

### 4. Security
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] Tenant isolation enforced
- [ ] Input validation present
- [ ] Authorization checks in place

### 5. Observability
- [ ] Structured logging with context
- [ ] Metrics for important operations
- [ ] Span created for traceable operations

### 6. Code Quality
- [ ] No compiler warnings
- [ ] No TODOs without issue links
- [ ] Follows patterns from LLD documentation
- [ ] No copy-pasted code

## Commit Message Format

```
type(scope): subject

body (optional)

Refs: #issue-number or US-XX.YY
```

**Types:** feat, fix, refactor, test, docs, chore
**Scope:** service name or component

```
feat(pipeline-service): implement pipeline creation

- Add Pipeline aggregate with event sourcing
- Add PipelineRepository with RLS support
- Add integration tests with Testcontainers

Refs: US-01.01
```

## Pull request title (before opening / updating a PR)

CI runs `amannn/action-semantic-pull-request` (see `.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml`). The PR title must:

- Use conventional form: `type(optional-scope): Subject here`
- Have the **subject start with an uppercase letter** (regex `^[A-Z].+$` on the subject only)

Example: `feat(execution-service): Cancel execution API (US-02.04)` — not `...: cancel execution ...`.

## Red Flags - Do NOT Commit If:

- ❌ Tests are failing
- ❌ You don't understand why the code works
- ❌ You're copying code without understanding it
- ❌ There's a TODO without an issue link
- ❌ You're adding a dependency not in ADRs
- ❌ Error handling is missing or empty
- ❌ No tests for new code
